        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Wonderful Opportunity in the Heart of Barntown\r\n\r\nDetached Bungalow | Mature Private Site | Excellent Location | Approx. 5 km from Wexford Town\r\n\r\nSituated in the highly regarded and sought-after village of Barntown, this charming detached bungalow, constructed circa 1976, occupies a mature and private site in an enviable residential setting.\r\n\r\nCarefully maintained over the years, the property offers generous, well-proportioned accommodation throughout and represents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to modernise and transform the house into a superb contemporary family home.\r\n\r\nApproached through established gardens, the property enjoys a wonderful sense of privacy and tranquillity, complemented by ample off-street parking. Its spacious proportions, mature setting and excellent location combine to offer significant potential for those seeking a home they can personalise and make their own.\r\n\r\nAn Exceptional Location\r\n\r\nBarntown is renowned for its welcoming community atmosphere and excellent range of local amenities. The village and surrounding area offer a wonderful balance between countryside living and everyday convenience, with Barntown National School, Glynn-Barntown GAA Club, local churches, cafés, convenience stores and scenic walking routes all close by.\r\n\r\nThe surrounding countryside provides numerous opportunities to enjoy the outdoors, with the spectacular Three Rocks and Forth Mountain areas nearby. A number of popular attractions are also within easy reach, including Johnstown Castle Estate and the Irish National Heritage Park.\r\n\r\nFor commuters and those requiring access to local services, the property is particularly well positioned. Wexford General Hospital and the M11/N25 road network are readily accessible, while Wexford Town is approximately 5 km away.\r\n\r\nWexford Town & Beyond\r\n\r\nWexford Town offers an extensive range of amenities, including excellent shopping, supermarkets, restaurants, cafés, primary and secondary schools, sporting facilities and a vibrant cultural scene. The town is home to the renowned National Opera House, while both rail and bus services provide convenient connections to surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nFor those travelling further afield, Rosslare Europort is approximately 22 km away, offering regular ferry services to the UK and continental Europe.\r\n\r\nA Home with Enormous Potential\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a detached bungalow on a mature private site in one of County Wexford's most desirable residential locations.\r\n\r\nWith its generous accommodation, established gardens, peaceful setting and superb connectivity, the property offers the incoming purchaser the opportunity to create a wonderful family home in a location that combines the best of village and town living.\r\n\r\nA property with character, space and considerable potential — ideally positioned just minutes from Wexford Town and all that the South East has to offer.\r\n\r\nVIEWING IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED."
      },
